      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Given the equations:\n1. \\( ab + bc + cd + da = 30 \\)\n2. \\( b + d = 5 \\)\n\nWe need to find the value of \\( a + c \\).\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the first equation by factoring out common terms:\n\\[ ab + bc + cd + da = b(a + c) + d(a + c) \\]\n\nSince \\( b + d = 5 \\), we can substitute \\( b + d \\) in the equation:\n\\[ b(a + c) + d(a + c) = (b + d)(a + c) = 5(a + c) \\]\n\nGiven that \\( ab + bc + cd + da = 30 \\), we substitute this into the equation:\n\\[ 5(a + c) = 30 \\]\n\nNow, solve for \\( a + c \\):\n\\[ a + c = \\frac{30}{5} = 6 \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( a + c \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]",
